---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons search -h <==
Find addons by name in the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub

Usage: omaddons search [OPTIONS] <QUERY>...

Arguments:
  <QUERY>...
          What to look for: words of the addon's name, folders, author or description

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>
          Consult only this source (repeatable): catalog, wowi, tukui or github
          
          [possible values: catalog, wowi, tukui, github]

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Most results to list (default 20, at most 50)

      --refresh
          Fetch the WoWInterface index and the Tukui list now, even inside their windows

Global options:
      --json
          One JSON envelope on stdout

      --robot
          The same as --json

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [possible values: json, human]

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the Classic Era client),
          family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every client)
          
          [alias: --flavor]

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change nothing)

      --actor <ACTOR>
          Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]

      --reason <TEXT>
          Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by commands that change
          nothing)

      --offline
          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]

      --while-running
          Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)

      --if-match <TOKEN>
          Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that returned this token
          (data.precondition) showed

      --no-color
          No ANSI color

      --no-progress
          No progress output

      --progress <MODE>
          Progress events on stderr
          
          [possible values: json, human, none]

      --quiet
          Only errors on stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          More detail (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Show help

Examples:
  omaddons search details           the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub at once
  omaddons find elvui --source tukui
  omaddons search bags --offline    what this machine already knows

Only GitHub's search receives the query; the catalog, the WoWInterface index and
the Tukui list are searched on this machine. Compatibility per client is a hint:
install verifies each addon's TOC.
